    "sentence_translations": [
      "Do you like to release pigeons?",
      "",
      "“She had a date with me today, but she never came. I was stood up again.”",
      "The “release a pigeon” in this sentences does not mean that you set free doves, ..",
      ".. but means that you do not honor an agreement, or miss an appointment.",
      "",
      "How come “releasing a pigeon” has this meaning?",
      "A long time ago, everyone used pigeons to communicate.",
      "Once, two people made an appointment to send each other letters.",
      "But one of them just released the pigeon without writing any letter.",
      "The other one said: “How can you just release the pigeon, and not honor our agreement?”",
      "And like that, the phrase “release a pigeon” appeared.",
      "",
      "You can use it in the following ways: “You better not stand me up”, “I was stood up by her five times”",
      "If you hear someone say that you like to release pigeons, it is certainly not a good thing."
    ]
